{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07X3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$q : \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-approximation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-product-effective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ad3f32bdcae108dbc0e549242a2a9d4b38003a4f868f15511d74a3eee661104d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:16494fb605db6a23f13b3f9021700718422425a95900b2429c13edace7a4a21c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003> be <MATH_0004>-morphisms of categories\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>. If the functor\n(<REF_0001>) is an equivalence for \n<MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007>, and <MATH_0008>, then it is \nan equivalence for <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7caa70a319b4eb80a6257c01bcb60d602a01d34546976274fb9addc0e759696f", "unit_id": "tag:07X9:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07X3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0006": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-approximation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-approximation}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{categories-lemma-equivalence-2-fibre-product}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2885ede752a2c84b554d826cc01bf8cde81e251a93ecb13d0a02cc32a08ff825", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c766a3fa91f64f9e502f8f873bf6fb5642aac960745f77874b5fcd326af4e03", "source_text": "The left and the right hand side of (<REF_0001>)\nfor <MATH_0001> are simply the <MATH_0002>-fibre\nproducts of the left and the right hand side of (<REF_0002>)\nfor <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>.\nHence the result follows as taking <MATH_0006>-fibre products is compatible\nwith equivalences of categories, see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dd4d83b60ffa3a8d014f506bbd0e5db8db09ffe0e2a4fa1af3215a8aaadbcdd0", "unit_id": "tag:07X9:proof"}
